{"name":"Mecha Kitty","hex":"#d0c4d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mecha","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large armoured robot on legs, typically controlled by a pilot seated inside."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mecha"},{"term":"kitty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young cat; a kitten.","A young cat; a kitten."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of jack (“a small, typically white, ball used as the target ball in bowls”).","A pool of money to which card players contribute a portion of their winnings, which is used for paying shared expenses such as the cost of the premises or refreshments;  any pool of money to which people contribute for shared expenses or other joint purposes; also, any fund of liquid assets set aside for future use.\n\nSynonym of pot (“a quantity of money available to be won in a round or a game”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mecha","blocks":[{"text":"In science fiction, mecha  or mechs are giant robots or machines, either depicted as piloted or sentient and are typically humanoid walking vehicles. The term was first used in Japanese after shortening the English loanword 'mechanism'  or 'mechanical' , but the meaning in Japanese is more inclusive, meaning any mechanism in general, and 'robot'  or 'giant robot' is the narrower term referring to robots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/%E3%82%AF%E3%83%A9%E3%82%BF%E3%82%B9%E3%83%BBMaker_Faire_Tokyo_2012_%281%29.jpg/330px-%E3%82%AF%E3%83%A9%E3%82%BF%E3%82%B9%E3%83%BBMaker_Faire_Tokyo_2012_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mecha","wikidata":"Q858784"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/%E5%95%A6%E5%95%A6%E5%AF%B6%E9%83%BD%E4%B8%8A%E6%B5%B7%E9%87%91%E6%A9%8B%E7%9A%84%E9%AB%98%E9%81%94%E6%A8%A1%E5%9E%8B